# ============================================================================
#  LINE ENDINGS ARE LOAD-BEARING HERE.
#
#  Every text file in this project is CRLF, and the ini is read by a CLEO
#  script rather than by a text editor that shrugs at line endings. Without
#  explicit rules git would normalise to LF in the repository and hand back
#  whatever the cloner's core.autocrlf happens to say.
#
#  Explicit eol=crlf, not `text=auto`: the point is that every checkout is
#  identical, not merely self-consistent on one machine.
# ============================================================================

*.md    text eol=crlf
*.ini   text eol=crlf
*.txt   text eol=crlf
*.yml   text eol=crlf

# Compiled CLEO scripts and game assets - never touch these.
*.cs    binary
*.txd   binary
*.png   binary

# ============================================================================
#  KEPT OUT OF THE RELEASE ZIP.
#
#  Every GitHub Release carries an auto-generated "Source code (zip)" built from
#  the tag with git archive, and that is what most people will download. These
#  three are repository plumbing - nobody installing the mod needs them, and a
#  hidden .github folder in a mod download just invites questions.
#
#  COVER.png and PSEUDOCODE.md go too: the cover is for the repo page and the
#  social preview, and the pseudocode is for people reading the project on
#  GitHub, not for someone installing the mod. The download is then exactly two
#  things - the Readme, and the folder it tells you to drag into modloader.
# ============================================================================

/.github        export-ignore
/.gitignore     export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/COVER.png      export-ignore
/PSEUDOCODE.md  export-ignore
